{"availability":"available","full":"Chemaclass/agnostic-ai","name":"agnostic-ai","description":"One source to rule them all: write agents, skills, rules, and hooks once, then sync them to your AI tools.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":23,"forks":5,"created":"2026-05-03T18:47:55Z","updated":"2026-10-08T15:58:20Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://agnostic-ai.org","topics":["agentic-ai","agents-md","agnostic-ai","ai-agents","claude","claude-code","cli","codex","copilot","cursor","developer-tools","gemini","golang","mcp"],"demo":"https://agnostic-ai.org/playground/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:03:19.775Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:03:19.775Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:03:19.775Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:40.129Z","stars":21,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:15:58.497Z","stars":21,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-06T15:43:22.830Z","stars":22,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-08T16:03:19.775Z","stars":23,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["agnostic-ai is for developers and teams using more than one AI coding tool, or preparing to change tools. Write agents, skills, rules, hooks, and MCP configuration once; agnostic-ai sync turns those specs into each tool's native files. See Why agnostic-ai.","Each AI tool reads its instructions from different files. Kept by hand, those files drift apart. agnostic-ai keeps one editable source in plain Markdown and YAML inside your repository. No account, no service.","Support spans Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, Copilot, Kiro, and more. Each tool supports a different set of spec kinds; the target reference shows the exact paths."],"features":["Rules, agents, skills, and commands in one spec format. Kiro commands land in .kiro/prompts/ for CLI V3.","Capabilities such as read(src/), shell(git diff ), and mcp:github map to each tool's own names. lint warns when one covers a whole tool. See Capabilities.","Model tiers name roles once for every tool. See Models and aliases.","MCP servers keep secrets as references, never literal values. See MCP references.","Session handoffs carry a task from one tool to another on the same machine. builtins: [handoff] adds the skill; handoff-hook adds Git snapshots and resume notices. See Session handoffs."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a2afd93f63cc5f196ed518658dac373e9504227772124cc87b62026beb45db66","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:45:41.605Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:45:41.605Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"agnostic-ai is for developers and teams using more than one AI coding tool, or preparing to change tools. Write agents, skills, rules, hooks, and MCP configuration once; agnostic-ai sync turns those specs into each tool's native files. See Why agnostic-ai.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No account, no service.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"a2afd93f63cc5f196ed518658dac373e9504227772124cc87b62026beb45db66","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T23:45:41.605Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T15:58:20Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T23:45:41.606Z","hash":"a2afd93f63cc5f196ed518658dac373e9504227772124cc87b62026beb45db66","originalBytes":6099,"storedBytes":6099,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["agnostic-ai","sync","tool","memory","one","see","agent","claude","project","cursor","each","existing","files","mcp","shared","adds","agents.md","bash","check","cli","code","codex","coding","commands","drift","every","files.","git","keeps","kiro","lint","make","native","once","rules",